/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050996 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186124510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050996 #edb/ref 1031 "The Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050996 #edb/ref 1033 1868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050996 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7821b684-8118-5d42-9459-ebb20010e0ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186121332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186121335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121331 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "36cf5fde-aae3-5ac2-808d-cd031ad46138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121332 #edb/ref 1080 "n" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121332 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121332 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8cade90-de90-5cc5-a96f-4b62957e1afc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121335 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121335 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121335 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6b1a034d-0611-5f21-a47f-fb41d7d10986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124320 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5424" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124320 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, and \n![](images/6a/6a294de4a5f2ff5755d8ceb5b91bb8920685a1cf2b5e727c5b5fdcfaaf0b89b0.svg)\n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^4$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "266a9a4e-cb11-5e4a-a2ac-c2e734966372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124320 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following: \n\n![](images/4b/4b42fd4ec8ccf491a1244a648af6fe40ce846fad388685e36d499783a095f8f7.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n![](images/32/327a582d15b82ebccda48358062310e6ad5c3bb2689f2024d76a8f8e7e1401a0.svg)\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\nSo,  according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since the matrix $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{Col}(A) \\neq \\mathbb{R}^4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{rank}(A) \\neq 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124433 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9961" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124433 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\det(A) = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124433 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124433 #edb/ref 1074 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible ![](images/dc/dc72aea1969143a926fd637d3360bb42116b27545a748923069f4ae732bd700f.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\det(A) = 0.$* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nSince $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n.$* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124434 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9962" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124434 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/3e/3e58a5f09c9060932ee854feeec0733dc9432c2de658308e3ebdccdd0ef89e5f.svg)\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. What should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124434 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fff1daf8-5a1f-54c9-90d7-87710ca00d23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124434 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/21/21455a41af5743da6f9f4de5e267c17c6037b929a01ba894cfd91530dbb39986.svg)\n\nThe missing expression is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124511 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1039 "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124629 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1039 "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124630 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1045 "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186125390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124685 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "6257a384-69ce-502a-8a3f-5b199a93b00a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124789 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186121331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124789 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140766" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124789 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124789 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124789 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b33961fd-1191-51c9-841c-0bdd04b0318b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124789 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\{0\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125390 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125390 #edb/ref 1061 19988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125390 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4620379b-2eed-5dd7-bf3a-9edf0b4aea79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125390 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125391 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125391 #edb/ref 1061 19991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125391 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "77230797-e80e-5644-8b1e-9e3722a0b66d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125391 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125591 #edb/ref 1061 37508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ebf299f-89ad-55ae-8fe6-d0af3bc56dfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125592 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125592 #edb/ref 1061 37509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125592 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "debf1d2f-c0e6-5c61-b195-a95710e2c35e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125592 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125780 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we are given an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ invertible matrix $A.$ Remember that if $A$ is invertible, then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution $\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nLet's extract all possible information from this fact using the vector spaces related to the matrix, namely, the *column space* and the *null space*.\n\n- The fact that the unique solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is $\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ tells us that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Null}(A)=\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\},\n$$\n\n or alternatively, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)) = \\textrm{nullity}(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Furthermore, if $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=0$ then $A$ has no *non-pivot* columns, or equivalently, all the columns of $A$ are *pivot columns*. So \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n- Finally, since $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ and its basis has $n$ linearly independent vectors, we can conclude that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^n.\n$$\n\nAll the results mentioned above can be summarized in the following theorem, called the **invertible matrix theorem**:\n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/7e/7ef5d72a30dd7f79f6182c4d78d705a7771f9f90ff0bb50f6d539614cb1e5b4d.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125780 #edb/ref 1065 3522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125780 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "555ca00c-d37e-5c67-a658-69b087390920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125780 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269419 #edb/ref 1080 "det(I-{A}^{n})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269419 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269419 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10dd7d25-8cfc-52a1-acc2-3277c8eeb2cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269574 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{Col}({A}^{n})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269574 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269574 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "22f60b50-9d54-5d0c-bd92-26d69595fd5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270689 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{Col}(A)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270689 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270689 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9fc3a383-4f66-5f23-a4b0-402cfefdcb88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270802 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{Col}({A}^{-1})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270802 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270802 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "abdc186b-e8ae-5ad6-90c7-9f9264cfc7a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271482 #edb/ref 1080 "det({A}^{n})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271482 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271482 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd18314a-6226-54bc-8252-cb6f9e346896" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186271482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186270689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271608 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "34c48b4c-89fa-5a1f-9048-8c8927a71839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272337 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272337 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142357" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272337 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272337 