#uuid "a5a3d425-a91c-5c69-83f8-fb2c7b092295" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328773 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328773 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328773 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d140b502-8ea3-591c-b1b5-620e9e563979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186328773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329188 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "01e66aa9-8412-5e42-8df8-d0eb8bcf68b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329820 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329820 #edb/ref 1069 "q-47587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329820 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329820 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329820 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c600e13-fdff-5526-82d0-6659ac10dfc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329820 #edb/ref 1074 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426033 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426033 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426033 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c95950f-0823-5370-bdc6-01bb92a952d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426034 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d6fe511-51db-512e-9712-3fce9ffdbf74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426035 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426035 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426035 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "114ef65a-d282-56b9-8b1c-7327abc02824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426036 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426036 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426036 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13e3d0a6-c269-5dde-bafd-a91861927c14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426037 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 175